# rdfs:comment overlay for data/wittgensteiniana_final.ttl.
# Contains ONLY the additional rdfs:comment triples; the base file is not
# modified.
# Comment sources (verified, no invented text):
#   - classes Thesis / TextFragment / Author: docstrings of the
#     original normalization layer and Pasin's Django sources
#     (TextUnit = the proposition units, typed schema:Chapter in the
#     official export; the separate ex:Thesis class was dropped as a
#     redundant duplicate layer of the same individuals),
#     tractatusapp models in Michele Pasin's Wittgensteiniana
#     (https://github.com/lambdamusic/wittgensteiniana,
#     src/apps/tractatusapp/models.py);
#   - schema.org terms and properties: canonical definitions from
#     https://schema.org/;
#   - local properties hasAuthor / hasTextFragment: derived from their
#     domain/range axioms in the base file.
# Usage: parse wittgensteiniana_final.ttl and this file into the same
# rdflib Graph.

@prefix ex: <http://example.org/wittgensteiniana/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .

ex:Author rdfs:comment "An author of a text expression. The official export records authorship as literal schema:author values; this class reifies those values as resources with rdfs:label."@en .

ex:TextFragment rdfs:comment "A fragment of an expression in FRBR terms: the symbolic contents of a text unit. If the symbols are organized using a code, that code (for example a language) can be specified too. Corresponds to TextFragment in Pasin's Django model and to schema:CreativeWork in the official RDF export (there typed as the fragment's additional schema:CreativeWork typing)."@en .

ex:hasAuthor rdfs:comment "Relates a book to one of its authors. Local replacement for the literal schema:author values used in the official export."@en .

ex:hasTextFragment rdfs:comment "Relates a text unit (schema:Chapter) to one of its text fragments. Inverse of schema:exampleOfWork."@en .

schema:Book rdfs:comment "A book. In this dataset: the Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus (the German original) and its two English editions (Ogden 1922; Pears and McGuinness 1961)."@en .

schema:Chapter rdfs:comment "One of the sections into which a book is divided. A chapter usually has a section number or a name. In this dataset every numbered Tractatus proposition, at every nesting level, is exported as a schema:Chapter."@en .

schema:CreativeWork rdfs:comment "The most generic kind of creative work, including books, movies, photographs, software programs, etc. In this dataset used for the text fragments (one per proposition per edition/language)."@en .

schema:DefinedTerm rdfs:comment "A word, name, acronym, phrase, etc. with a formal definition. Often used in the context of category or subject classification, glossaries or dictionaries, product or creative work types, etc. Use the name property for the term being defined, use termCode if the term has an alpha-numeric code allocated, use description to provide the definition of the term. In this dataset: a philosophical concept from the legacy OCML classification."@en .

schema:DefinedTermSet rdfs:comment "A set of defined terms, for example a set of categories or a classification scheme, a glossary, dictionary or enumeration. In this dataset: the Wittgensteiniana concept classification."@en .

schema:datePublished rdfs:comment "Date of first publication or broadcast. For example the date a CreativeWork was broadcast or a Certification was issued."@en .

schema:description rdfs:comment "A description of the item. Used here for the definition of a concept (schema:DefinedTerm)."@en .

schema:exampleOfWork rdfs:comment "A creative work that this work is an example/instance/realization/derivation of."@en .

schema:inDefinedTermSet rdfs:comment "A DefinedTermSet that contains this term."@en .

schema:inLanguage rdfs:comment "The language of the content or performance or used in an action. Please use one of the language codes from the IETF BCP 47 standard. See also availableLanguage."@en .

schema:isPartOf rdfs:comment "Indicates an item or CreativeWork that this item, or CreativeWork (in some sense), is part of."@en .

schema:mentions rdfs:comment "Indicates that the CreativeWork contains a reference to, but is not necessarily about a concept."@en .

schema:name rdfs:comment "The name of the item."@en .

schema:position rdfs:comment "The position of an item in a series or sequence of items."@en .

schema:text rdfs:comment "The textual content of this CreativeWork."@en .

schema:translationOfWork rdfs:comment "The work that this work has been translated from."@en .

